msgid "Triton算子开发指南"
msgstr "Triton Operator Development Guide"

msgid "概述：本文着重介绍了在NPU上进行Triton算子开发中值得注意的问题，分为三个方面：多核任务并行、单核数据搬运、单核数据运算。首先在多核任务并行中介绍了设置最大硬件核数的依据以及具体的实现。然后在单核数据搬运中具体描述了如何设置合适的循环内数据分块大小，并且介绍了过程中常用的优化手段，还补充了可能面临的UB OVERFLOW问题的处理方式。最后回归单个算子，在单核数据运算层面着重介绍了如何开发Triton算子，并强调了相关的关键点。"
msgstr "Overview: This article focuses on notable issues in Triton operator development on NPU, divided into three aspects: multi-core task parallelism, single-core data movement, and single-core data computation. First, it introduces the basis for setting the maximum number of hardware cores and the specific implementation in multi-core task parallelism. Then, it details how to set an appropriate data chunk size within loops during single-core data movement, introduces common optimization techniques used in the process, and supplements the handling of potential UB OVERFLOW issues. Finally, it returns to a single operator, focusing on how to develop Triton operators at the single-core data computation level, and emphasizes the relevant key points."

msgid "文档组织"
msgstr "Document Organization"

msgid "本指南将通用开发原则和按硬件执行单元划分的算子开发路径分开组织："
msgstr "This guide separates general development principles from operator development paths organized by hardware execution units:"

msgid "本页介绍所有 Triton-Ascend 算子都需要关注的通用问题，包括分核、片上内存、访存、Tiling 和 Autotune。"
msgstr "This page introduces common issues that all Triton-Ascend operators need to pay attention to, including core partitioning, on-chip memory, memory access, Tiling, and Autotune."

msgid "[Vector 算子开发](./vector_operator.md) 介绍主要由 Vector Core 执行的逐元素、归约、Gather/Scatter 等算子。"
msgstr "[Vector Operator Development](./vector_operator.md) introduces operators such as element-wise, reduction, Gather/Scatter, etc., primarily executed by the Vector Core."

msgid "[Cube 算子开发](./cube_operator.md) 介绍以 `tl.dot`、矩阵乘、批量矩阵乘为核心的算子。"
msgstr "[Cube Operator Development](./cube_operator.md) introduces operators centered around `tl.dot`, matrix multiplication, and batched matrix multiplication."

msgid "[CV 融合算子开发](./cv_fusion_operator.md) 介绍同一个算子中同时存在 Cube 计算和 Vector 后处理、归约、Softmax 或跨核协同的场景。"
msgstr "[CV Fusion Operator Development](./cv_fusion_operator.md) introduces scenarios where Cube computation and Vector post-processing, reduction, Softmax, or cross-core collaboration coexist within the same operator."

msgid "简单算子优先参考本仓 `docs/zh/examples/` 和 `third_party/ascend/tutorials/`；复杂算子优先参考 GitHub 上的 [Ascend/triton-ascend-ops](https://github.com/Ascend/triton-ascend-ops) 中 `tutorial/best_practice/` 的完整优化案例。"
msgstr "For simple operators, refer primarily to `docs/zh/examples/` and `third_party/ascend/tutorials/` in this repository; for complex operators, refer primarily to the complete optimization cases in `tutorial/best_practice/` under [Ascend/triton-ascend-ops](https://github.com/Ascend/triton-ascend-ops) on GitHub."

msgid "通用多核任务并行"
msgstr "Generic multi-core task parallelism"

msgid "设置最大硬件核数"
msgstr "Set the maximum number of hardware cores."

msgid "在一个Triton算子中，通常使用grid进行分核操作。对于GPU而言，其计算核心SM通常是几十到几百量级。但是对于昇腾 NPU 平台而言，其计算核心AI Core的数量在几十个的量级。 虽然运行时接口允许下发并发任务数最大为65535，但超过物理核数的部分是通过新一轮的下发来完成的。如果直接将GPU上的Triton算子拿到昇腾平台上运行，这些大量的任务会引入可观的核启动和核初始化时的额外开销，影响到算子性能表现。 因此，需要针对昇腾平台特性修改分核逻辑。最推荐的做法是**将分核的数量直接固定为硬件的物理核数**，在核内做更为细致的数据分块："
msgstr "In a Triton operator, the grid is typically used for kernel partitioning. For GPUs, the number of compute cores (SMs) is usually on the order of tens to hundreds. However, for the Ascend NPU platform, the number of compute cores (AI Cores) is on the order of tens. Although the runtime interface allows a maximum of 65535 concurrent tasks to be dispatched, the portion exceeding the physical core count is completed through additional dispatch rounds. If Triton operators from GPUs are directly run on the Ascend platform, these numerous tasks will introduce considerable overhead from kernel launch and kernel initialization, impacting operator performance. Therefore, the kernel partitioning logic needs to be modified to suit the characteristics of the Ascend platform. The most recommended approach is to **fix the number of kernels directly to the hardware's physical core count** and perform finer-grained data partitioning within each kernel."

msgid "<br />\\n"
msgstr "<br />"

msgid "\\\\\\n"
msgstr "\\\\\\n"

msgid "对于纯Vector算子，分核数等于**Vector核数量**"
msgstr "For pure Vector operators, the number of sub-cores equals the **number of Vector cores**."

msgid "对于CV融合算子，分核数等于**Cube核数量**（通常为Vector核数量的一半），算子执行时会按1：2的比例调用Vector核"
msgstr "For the CV fusion operator, the number of split cores equals the **number of Cube cores** (usually half the number of Vector cores). When the operator executes, it invokes Vector cores in a 1:2 ratio."

msgid "一般而言，在NPU卡上，一个计算核心AI Core含有一个cube核，每个cube核配有两个vector核，因此可以通过以下接口获取**Vector核数(vectorcore_num)**与**Cube核数量(aicore_num)**："
msgstr "Generally, on an NPU card, a computing core AI Core contains one cube core, and each cube core is equipped with two vector cores. Therefore, the **number of vector cores (vectorcore_num)** and the **number of cube cores (aicore_num)** can be obtained through the following interfaces:"

msgid "import torch\\n"
msgstr "import torch"

msgid "参考示例代码，先固定核数，再通过内部循环分批处理任务分块："
msgstr "Refer to the sample code, first fix the number of cores, then process task chunks in batches through an inner loop:"

msgid "NUM_CORE = vectorcore_num\\n"
msgstr "NUM_CORE = vectorcore_num"

msgid "通用单核数据搬运"
msgstr "General single-core data transfer"

msgid "设置合适的循环内数据分块大小（BLOCK SIZE）"
msgstr "Set an appropriate data block size (BLOCK SIZE) for the loop."

msgid "以add_kernel为例，变量和操作共同决定了片上内存空间的占用大，通过修改BLOCK_SIZE大小可以调整循环内数据分块和计算中间结果占用的大小。如果超过上限则算子编译时会提示预期占用大小并报错。要达到最大计算访存比，BLOCK_SIZE需要在不超出片上空间时尽可能大，这可以通过Triton-Ascend的[Autotune](../examples/06_autotune_example.md)预先设置不同的BLOCK_SIZE，运行时会自动选取最优设置。"
msgstr "Taking `add_kernel` as an example, variables and operations together determine the on-chip memory space usage. By modifying the `BLOCK_SIZE`, you can adjust the size of data blocks within the loop and the intermediate result usage. If it exceeds the upper limit, the operator compilation will report the expected usage size and raise an error. To achieve the maximum compute-to-memory-access ratio, `BLOCK_SIZE` should be as large as possible without exceeding the on-chip space. This can be achieved by pre-setting different `BLOCK_SIZE` values using Triton-Ascend's [Autotune](../examples/06_autotune_example.md), and the runtime will automatically select the optimal setting."

msgid "import triton.language as tl\\n"
msgstr "import triton.language as tl"

msgid "尽量保证Tensor的尾轴（最后一个维度）大小数据对齐"
msgstr "Try to ensure that the size data of the Tensor's trailing axis (the last dimension) is aligned."

msgid "【描述】对于VV类算子需要调用Vector核计算时，昇腾硬件的UB要求Tensor的尾轴（最后一个维度）大小能被32Byte整除，而对于CV类算子需要调用vector核和Cube核计算时，要求Tensor的尾轴大小能被512Byte整除，若尾轴长度不足则会自动补齐。在此前提下，对模型中shape为(2048,3)和(2048,1)Tensor的种种操作，都会因为自动补齐导致性能明显恶化，此时可考虑通过转置操作将对齐轴转到低维，直到store时再转置为原始状态，从而规避自动补齐，优化计算速度。同时由于转置操作本身也受自动补齐规则的影响，因此同样需要特殊技巧来规避补齐。这里列出一个\"借轴转置\"的tip，适用于**tensor.numel() % 256Byte == 0**的场景，具体操作如下："
msgstr "【Description】For VV-type operators that need to invoke the Vector core for computation, the UB of Ascend hardware requires that the size of the tensor's last axis (the final dimension) be divisible by 32 bytes. For CV-type operators that need to invoke both the Vector core and the Cube core, the tensor's last axis size must be divisible by 512 bytes. If the last axis length is insufficient, it will be automatically padded. Under this premise, various operations on tensors with shapes (2048,3) and (2048,1) in the model will experience significant performance degradation due to automatic padding. In such cases, consider using transpose operations to move the alignment axis to a lower dimension, and only transpose back to the original state at store time, thereby avoiding automatic padding and optimizing computation speed. Additionally, since the transpose operation itself is also affected by the automatic padding rule, special techniques are also needed to avoid padding. Here is a \"borrowed-axis transpose\" tip, applicable to scenarios where **tensor.numel() % 256Byte == 0**, with the specific operations as follows:"

msgid "注：VV类算子表示该类算子在运算过程中只使用了Vector Core；CV类算子表示该类算子运算过程中既使用了AI Core又使用了Vector Core。"
msgstr "Note: VV-type operators indicate that such operators only use the Vector Core during computation; CV-type operators indicate that such operators use both the AI Core and the Vector Core during computation."

msgid "示例"
msgstr "Example"

msgid "# conv_state = tensor([2048, 3], bfloat16)\\n"
msgstr "# conv_state = tensor([2048, 3], bfloat16)"

msgid "先将数据搬运到UB上，再从UB中select目标值"
msgstr "First move the data to UB, then select the target value from UB."

msgid "【描述】在NPU的离散场景下，可以先将数据搬运到UB，再从share中select目标值。"
msgstr "【Description】In the discrete scenario of the NPU, data can first be moved to the UB, and then the target value can be selected from the share."

msgid "@triton.jit\\n"
msgstr "@triton.jit"

msgid "优化前后性能分析和对比"
msgstr "Performance analysis and comparison before and after optimization"

msgid "通过msprof工具执行用例可得到PROF_*文件夹，里面包含了op_summary_\\*.csv文件，该文件可以帮助分析流水情况。注：“\\*”表示时间戳，[性能数据采集参考方法](../debug_guide/profiling.md)。"
msgstr "Running test cases with the msprof tool generates a PROF_* folder, which contains the op_summary_\\*.csv file. This file helps analyze pipeline conditions. Note: \"\\*\" represents a timestamp, [refer to the performance data collection method](../debug_guide/profiling.md)."

